Notebook[{Cell["Transverse spin transfer in proton-proton collisions, step 5: \
the generalized crossing from p^ p^ -> c + X", "Title"], 
  Cell["Generalized crossing symmetry relates the transverse spin transfer \
cross sections to the double-transverse ones of Processes/HadronicTT: knowing \
a^ b^ -> c + X, the process a^ cbar -> bbar^ + X follows by s <-> t, v -> \
-v/(1-v), w unchanged, including the phase-space integration.  The \
implementation must account for log(v) -> log(-v/(1-v)), the pi^2 terms, the \
spin averaging factors and the interchange of the incoming-parton and \
fragmentation counterterms.  This step checks the crossing against the \
results of Processes/HadronicTT at LO (exactly) and at NLO (the complete \
finite coefficients), for every class of this process.  Input: \
Results/<route>/class-<n>/Algebra.wl of both processes (and Transfer.wl of \
this process for the NLO comparison); output: \
Results/<route>/crossing/class-<n>.wl per pair, and the pseudo-classes \
Results/<route>/class-<n>x/ described below.\n\nThe crossing.  The TT process \
a(pa) b(pb) -> c(p) + d(k1) [+ e(k2)] is crossed by b <-> cbar: pb -> -p and \
p -> -pb (the momenta of the transfer process), with the unobserved momenta \
k1, k2 unchanged.  The invariants: s <-> t, u unchanged, A = (pa-k1)^2 \
unchanged, B = (pb-k1)^2 <-> C = (p+k1)^2, spe3 (the hatted k1) unchanged; v \
= 1 + t/s -> -v/(1-v), w = -u/(s+t) unchanged.  The pairs (transfer class <- \
TT class; the unobserved parton k1 of the two class entries must coincide, \
which is checked on the species lists):\n\n   3 <- 5:    q qb -> qp (k1 = \
qpb)  -->  q qpb -> q + X;    11 <- 11:  q qb -> q (k1 = qb)  -->  q qb -> q \
+ X;    17 <- 6:  q q -> q  -->  q qb -> qb (= qb q -> q by charge \
conjugation, class 17);\n   13 <- 12:  q qb -> g  -->  q g -> q + X;    10 <- \
7:  q q -> g (NLO only)  -->  q g -> qb + X;\n   1 <- 5 and 6 <- 11 observe \
the antiquark of the TT pair: the TT process with the observed antiquark, q \
qb -> qpb (q qb -> qb), equals by charge conjugation the class's own square \
with a and b exchanged, pa <-> pb (t <-> u, A <-> B; checked in step 2 of \
HadronicTT on the Born table), so these two pairs use the composed map pa -> \
-p, pb -> pa, p -> -pb: s -> t, t -> u, u -> s, A -> C, B -> A, C -> \
B.\n\nThe constant factor.  Per pair the transfer square is a constant times \
the crossed TT square, component by component:\n\n   XX_transfer = - sigma g \
x XX_TT(crossed),   NN_transfer = + sigma g x NN_TT(crossed),   sigma = +1, g \
= 1 (b a quark or antiquark),   sigma = -1, g = 2 CA/((D-2)(CA^2-1)) = \
1/((D-2) CF) (b a gluon).\n\nDerivation.  (i) Spinor structures: the TT \
density of b, pb-slash gamma5 sb-slash/2, becomes -p-slash gamma5 sb-slash/2 \
at pb -> -p, while the transfer projection of the observed quark is p-slash \
gamma5 sc-slash (no 1/2); the TT spin sum of an observed quark, p-slash, \
becomes -pb-slash at p -> -pb, while the transfer's unpolarized quark b \
carries pb-slash/2: the product (-1/2)(-2) = 1 contains the two fermion \
crossing signs.  When the TT observed parton is a gluon (the pairs 13 <- 12 \
and 10 <- 7, whose transfer parton b is that gluon), its polarization sum is \
even in its momentum and the second sign is absent: sigma = -1 for these \
pairs, +1 otherwise.  (ii) Colour: the TT average 1/Nc^2 against the \
transfer's 1/Nc x 1/N_b with N_b = Nc (quark) or Nc^2 - 1 (gluon).  (iii) A \
TT gluon c is summed over its physical polarizations with the reference \
vector pa, and the transfer's incoming gluon b is averaged with the same sum, \
reference pa, and 1/(D-2); the sums coincide (the reference momentum enters \
as a ratio).  Together: sigma = 1, g = 1 for a quark b and sigma = -1, g = 2 \
Nc/((D-2)(Nc^2-1)) for a gluon b.  (iv) The axes.  The TT in-plane axis aX = \
p + (u/s) pa + (t/s) pb, crossed, is -pb + (u/t) pa - (s/t) p (transfer \
momenta), orthogonal to pa and p.  As the spin vector of a it equals (-s/t) \
eX + (2u/t) pa, where eX = (u/s) pa + (t/s) pb + p is the transfer's in-plane \
axis of a and the multiple of pa is annihilated by pa-slash gamma5; as the \
spin vector of c it equals -((t+u)/t) eC - 2 s u/(t (t+u)) p with the \
transfer's eC = -u/(t+u) pa + t/(t+u) pb - s (u-t)/(t+u)^2 p, the multiple of \
p annihilated by p-slash gamma5.  With the normalizations (TT divides by \
-aX^2 -> s u/t; the transfer by |eX| |eC| = -t u/(t+u)) the product of the \
two coefficients gives exactly -1: the crossed in-plane axis of b points \
along -eC (the azimuth map phi_b -> pi - phi_c).  The normal n ~ eps^{mu pa \
pb p} is reflected under the crossing, but both TT densities carry it: NN \
keeps its sign.  (v) Projections: TT's cos(2 Phi) coefficient TT = (XX-NN)/2 \
therefore crosses into -(XX+NN)/(2 sigma g) of the transfer (the coefficient \
of cos(phi_a - phi_c)), and TT's evanescent Symmetric = (XX+NN)/2 into \
-(XX-NN)/(2 sigma g), the difference of the two transfer components (not into \
their sum).  All signs and factors are fixed by this derivation and verified \
exactly on the D-dimensional Born terms of the six pairs with a Born term; \
for the NLO-only pair 10 <- 7 (a gluon b, like 13 <- 12 whose Born term \
verifies sigma and g including the D dependence) the same formula is used and \
is tested by the pole cancellation of Part B: its real-emission poles must \
cancel against the transfer counterterm P_{qb <- g} x Born(q qb -> \
qb)_transfer, which fixes the normalization including the gluon \
average.\n\nThe one-loop families.  The scalar integrals of the TT virtual \
interference are defined by their propagators; under the crossing VirtualST \
(s,t box) maps onto itself with the indices permuted (s <-> t), and VirtualSU \
<-> VirtualTU; for the composed map all three permute cyclically.  The map is \
found on the propagator sets by a shift and a reflection of the loop momentum \
(the integrals are invariant under both, the hatted loop momentum too) and \
verified to be a permutation of the family's propagators.  The integrals are \
then those of the transfer process with the transfer's Feynman prescription: \
the crossing is done before any integral is evaluated, and the real parts are \
taken in the transfer's physical region by step 3.\n\nPart A (exact, algebra \
level) compares, for every pair, the crossed TT objects of step 2 with those \
of this process: the Born squares and the complete Born table \
(rational-function identities in s, t, D, CA), the virtual XX and NN after \
the reduction to master integrals (term by term the scalar-integral \
coefficients agree only when both files route every graph onto the same \
family members, which is recorded; in general the two sides differ by \
integral identities, such as the same bubble written in two families), XX and \
NN modulo the integration identities that relate the two treatments of the \
normal component of the loop momentum (HadronicTT uses the exact identity \
(n.loop)^2 = loop_par^2 - loop^2 + loopHat2, this process the angular average \
-loop_perp^2/(D-3); both sides are brought to a common form by replacing \
every hatted power by its angular average, loopHat2^h -> \
((D-4)/2)_h/((D-3)/2)_h (loop_perp^2)^h, and reduced with Kira in D \
dimensions: the coefficients of the master integrals must agree exactly), and \
the real-emission squares (rational functions with tens of thousands of \
terms, compared exactly at random rational points of all invariants).\n\nPart \
B (the complete NLO check) writes the crossed TT algebra as a pseudo-class \
\"<n>x\" of this process (the transfer class's entry of classes.wl as its \
specification, the crossed TT Born table as its counterterm table, which Part \
A has shown to equal the transfer's) and runs steps 3 and 4 of this process \
on it, exactly as on a class of its own.  This implements generalized \
crossing symmetry at the level of phase-space integrals: the crossed \
integrands are integrated by step 3 in the transfer region (the phase-space \
masters at s4 = s v (1-w) of the transfer process, the loop masters continued \
in the transfer's s channel, with the real part taken there), so no finite TT \
expression is continued and no log(v) -> log(-v/(1-v)) or pi^2 term has to be \
tracked by hand; the counterterms are those of step 4 of this process \
(transversity kernels on leg a and on the fragmenting quark, unpolarized \
kernels on leg b with the lower transfer Born terms): this is the interchange \
of the incoming-parton and fragmentation counterterms, and the cancellation \
of the poles of the crossed integrals against them tests the crossing factors \
once more, including the pair without a Born term.  The finite coefficients \
{regular, D0, D1, delta} of both components of the pseudo-class must then \
equal those of the directly computed class, exactly at rational points of s, \
v, w, Nf with symbolic scales; the real-emission and virtual finite parts are \
compared separately as well.", "Text"], Cell["Load", "Section"], 
  Cell["Get[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \"..\", \"FeynFacet\", \
\"FeynFacet.wl\"}]]", "Input"], Cell["Choices: the route of the step-2 files; \
the transfer classes to check (\"all\", or a comma-separated list such as \
\"3,17\"; a class set through class = \"<n>\", as RunSteps[..., \
\"class=<n>\"] does, selects that one pair); the stage (\"A\": Part A and the \
pseudo-class algebra only; \"all\": also steps 3 and 4 of the pseudo-class, \
run here in fresh kernels when their results are missing, and the NLO \
comparison); and whether pseudo-class results of an earlier run of this file \
may be reused (\"no\" reruns steps 3 and 4).  Every pair reads the TT file \
Processes/HadronicTT/Results/<route>/class-<m>/Algebra.wl and this process's \
Algebra.wl (and, for the NLO comparison, Transfer.wl) of class <n>.", 
   "Text"], Cell["route = \"FeynCalc\";\nclass = \"\";                        \
          (* set by RunSteps[..., \"class=<n>\"]: the pair of that transfer \
class only *)\npairs = \"all\";\nstage = \"all\";\nreuse = \
\"yes\";\nGet[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \
\"classes.wl\"}]];\nttDirectory = FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"..\", \
\"HadronicTT\"}];\ncrossingTable = <|\n  \"1\" -> <|\"TT\" -> \"5\", \
\"Relabel\" -> True|>, \"3\" -> <|\"TT\" -> \"5\", \"Relabel\" -> False|>, \
\"6\" -> <|\"TT\" -> \"11\", \"Relabel\" -> True|>,\n  \"10\" -> <|\"TT\" -> \
\"7\", \"Relabel\" -> False|>, \"11\" -> <|\"TT\" -> \"11\", \"Relabel\" -> \
False|>, \"13\" -> <|\"TT\" -> \"12\", \"Relabel\" -> False|>,\n  \"17\" -> \
<|\"TT\" -> \"6\", \"Relabel\" -> False|>|>;\npairList = Which[class =!= \
\"\", {class}, pairs === \"all\", Keys[crossingTable], True, StringTrim /@ \
StringSplit[pairs, \",\"]];\nRequire[SubsetQ[Keys[crossingTable], pairList], \
\"Unknown transfer class in the pairs\", pairList];\ncrossingDirectory = \
ResultsDirectory[route <> \"/crossing\"];\nttAlgebraFile[m_] := \
FileNameJoin[{ttDirectory, \"Results\", route, \"class-\" <> m, \
\"Algebra.wl\"}];\ntransferFile[n_, name_] := \
FileNameJoin[{ResultsDirectory[route <> \"/class-\" <> n], name <> \
\".wl\"}];\npairList", "Input"], Cell["The crossing map", "Section"], 
  Cell["The momentum map of a pair (direct: pb -> -p, p -> -pb; composed with \
a <-> b for the pairs that observe the antiquark: pa -> -p, pb -> pa, p -> \
-pb) is turned into rules for the invariants by evaluating the squares \
(pa+pb)^2, (pa-p)^2, (pb-p)^2, (pa-k1)^2, (pb-k1)^2, (p+k1)^2 with the \
transfer's scalar products (the D-dimensional k1^2 = 0; spe3 is k1's own and \
unchanged).  The constant factor g and the sign sigma of the pair are read \
from the species of the transfer's parton b, and the signs of the components \
are those of the introduction.  The TT files hold the projections TT and \
Symmetric of the virtual and real parts; XX = TT + Symmetric and NN = \
Symmetric - TT are rebuilt (the Born holds all four).  The SU(N) relation CF \
= (CA^2-1)/(2 CA) is used in every exact comparison, since the colour factors \
of the two processes are written through CA and CF differently.", "Text"], 
  Cell["momentumMap[relabel_] := If[relabel, {pa -> -p, pb -> pa, p -> -pb}, \
{pa -> pa, pb -> -p, p -> -pb}];\nproducts = <|{pa, pb} -> s/2, {p, pa} -> \
-t/2, {p, pb} -> -u/2, {k1, pa} -> -A/2, {k1, pb} -> -B/2, {k1, p} -> C/2,\n  \
{loop, loop} -> L2, {loop, pa} -> Lpa, {loop, pb} -> Lpb, {loop, p} -> \
Lp|>;\nscalarProduct[x_, y_] := Lookup[products, Key[Sort[{x, y}]], 0];       \
       (* pa^2 = pb^2 = p^2 = k1^2 = 0 *)\nsquareOf[q_] := Module[{e = \
Expand[q], vectors = {pa, pb, p, k1, loop}},\n  Expand[Sum[Coefficient[e, x] \
Coefficient[e, y] scalarProduct[x, y], {x, vectors}, {y, \
vectors}]]];\ncrossingRules[map_] := {s -> squareOf[(pa + pb) /. map], t -> \
squareOf[(pa - p) /. map], u -> squareOf[(pb - p) /. map],\n  A -> \
squareOf[(pa - k1) /. map], B -> squareOf[(pb - k1) /. map], C -> squareOf[(p \
+ k1) /. map]};\ncolourRelation = CF -> (CA^2 - 1)/(2 CA);\nsigns = <|\"XX\" \
-> -1, \"NN\" -> 1|>;\ngluonFactor = 2 CA/((D - 2) (CA^2 - \
1));\ncrossingSign[b_] := If[b === \"g\", -1, 1];                     (* \
sigma: one fermion crossing sign is absent when the TT observed parton (the \
transfer's b) is a gluon *)\ncrossingFactor[b_] := If[b === \"g\", \
gluonFactor, 1];          (* g *)\nconjugate = <|\"q\" -> \"qb\", \"qb\" -> \
\"q\", \"qp\" -> \"qpb\", \"qpb\" -> \"qp\", \"g\" -> \
\"g\"|>;\npartonsOf[spec_] := (spec[\"Born\"] /. None -> spec[\"Real\"][[1, \
1]])[[1 ;; 4]];        (* {a, b, c, d}: d the unobserved parton k1 \
*)\nttComponents[object_] := <|\"XX\" -> object[\"TT\"] + \
object[\"Symmetric\"], \"NN\" -> object[\"Symmetric\"] - \
object[\"TT\"]|>;\nColumn[Table[n <> \" <- \" <> crossingTable[n][\"TT\"] <> \
\":  \" <> \
ToString[crossingRules[momentumMap[crossingTable[n][\"Relabel\"]]], \
InputForm], {n, Keys[crossingTable]}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["One pair: the two algebra files, the species check (the crossed TT \
species a, cbar, bbar, d must be the transfer's a, b, c, d; for the composed \
map the TT species are first exchanged a <-> b and conjugated, which is the \
charge-conjugation argument above), the invariant rules and the factor.", 
   "Text"], Cell["loadPair[n_] := Module[{entry = crossingTable[n], tt, \
transfer, spec, map, ttPartons, crossedPartons, b, g},\n  tt = \
Get[ttAlgebraFile[entry[\"TT\"]]];\n  transfer = Get[transferFile[n, \
\"Algebra\"]];\n  spec = HadronicTransferClasses[ToExpression[n]];\n  \
Require[spec[{\"Name\", \"Born\", \"Virtual\", \"Real\"}] === \
transfer[\"Spec\"][{\"Name\", \"Born\", \"Virtual\", \"Real\"}], \"The class \
entry differs from the one used by step 2\", n];\n  map = \
momentumMap[entry[\"Relabel\"]];\n  ttPartons = partonsOf[tt[\"Spec\"]];\n  \
If[entry[\"Relabel\"], ttPartons = conjugate /@ ttPartons[[{2, 1, 3, 4}]]];   \
                 (* a <-> b and charge conjugation: the same TT square *)\n  \
crossedPartons = {ttPartons[[1]], conjugate[ttPartons[[3]]], \
conjugate[ttPartons[[2]]], ttPartons[[4]]};\n  (* class 17 is written as the \
charge conjugate (qb q -> q) of the crossed process (q qb -> qb): the same \
square, checked in step 2 on the Born table *)\n  Require[crossedPartons === \
partonsOf[spec] || (conjugate /@ crossedPartons) === partonsOf[spec], \"The \
crossed TT species are not those of the transfer class (up to charge \
conjugation)\", {n, crossedPartons, partonsOf[spec]}];\n  b = \
partonsOf[spec][[2]];\n  <|\"Transfer\" -> n, \"TT\" -> entry[\"TT\"], \
\"Relabel\" -> entry[\"Relabel\"], \"Map\" -> map, \"Rules\" -> \
crossingRules[map], \"Factor\" -> crossingFactor[b], \"Sign\" -> \
crossingSign[b], \"Spec\" -> spec,\n    \"TTAlgebra\" -> tt, \
\"TransferAlgebra\" -> transfer, \"Name\" -> spec[\"Name\"] <> \"  <-  \" <> \
tt[\"Spec\"][\"Name\"] <> If[entry[\"Relabel\"], \" (observed antiquark, a \
<-> b)\", \"\"]|>];\ncrossObject[pair_, expr_, component_] := \
signs[component] pair[\"Sign\"] pair[\"Factor\"] (expr /. \
pair[\"Rules\"]);\nloaded = Association @ Table[n -> loadPair[n], {n, \
pairList}];\nColumn[Table[loaded[n][\"Name\"] <> \":  sigma = \" <> \
ToString[loaded[n][\"Sign\"]] <> \", g = \" <> \
ToString[loaded[n][\"Factor\"], InputForm], {n, pairList}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Part A: the Born terms and the Born table", "Section"], 
  Cell["The crossed TT Born square of the pair must equal the transfer's Born \
square in D dimensions, for XX and NN (classes without a Born term: both \
vanish), and the projections cross as stated: -sigma g x TT -> (XX+NN)/2, \
-sigma g x Symmetric -> (XX-NN)/2.  The complete transfer Born table follows \
from the TT table by the direct crossing of every channel, a b -> c (k1 = d) \
into a cbar -> bbar (k1 = d), with sigma and g of the species of cbar: the \
seven transfer channels of classes.wl are all obtained (qb q -> q from the TT \
channel qb qb -> qb).  At LO the relation can be written in terms of the hard \
cross sections b(v) = |M|^2 (4 Pi alphaS)^2/(16 Pi^2 s v) of step 4: since s' \
v' = s v under the crossing (s' = t = -s(1-v), v' = -v/(1-v)) and b is \
proportional to 1/s,\n\n   b_transfer,XX(v) = + sigma g \
b_TT,XX(-v/(1-v))/(1-v),   b_transfer,NN(v) = - sigma g \
b_TT,NN(-v/(1-v))/(1-v),   and at D = 4 both equal sigma g \
b_TT(-v/(1-v))/(1-v) with b_TT the cos(2 Phi) coefficient of HadronicTT \
(b_TT,XX = -b_TT,NN = b_TT there),\n\nan identity of rational functions of v, \
checked here with the D-dimensional Born squares of the two files (for the \
pairs 1 <- 5 and 6 <- 11, b_TT is that of the TT process with the observed \
antiquark, the class's own with t <-> u).", "Text"], 
  Cell["exactZero[expr_] := Factor[expr /. u -> -s - t /. colourRelation] === \
0;\nhard[square_] := square (4 Pi alphaS)^2/(16 Pi^2 s v);\nbornCheck[pair_] \
:= Module[{tt = pair[\"TTAlgebra\"], transfer = pair[\"TransferAlgebra\"], \
differences, projections, slide, table, tableDifferences},\n  differences = \
Association @ Table[comp -> exactZero[crossObject[pair, tt[\"Born\"][comp], \
comp] - transfer[\"Born\"][comp]], {comp, {\"XX\", \"NN\"}}];\n  Require[And \
@@ Values[differences], \"The crossed TT Born square differs from the \
transfer's\", {pair[\"Name\"], differences}];\n  projections = \
{exactZero[-pair[\"Sign\"] pair[\"Factor\"] (tt[\"Born\"][\"TT\"] /. \
pair[\"Rules\"]) - (transfer[\"Born\"][\"XX\"] + \
transfer[\"Born\"][\"NN\"])/2],\n    exactZero[-pair[\"Sign\"] \
pair[\"Factor\"] (tt[\"Born\"][\"Symmetric\"] /. pair[\"Rules\"]) - \
(transfer[\"Born\"][\"XX\"] - transfer[\"Born\"][\"NN\"])/2]};\n  \
Require[projections === {True, True}, \"The TT projections do not cross into \
-(XX+NN)/2 and -(XX-NN)/2\", pair[\"Name\"]];\n  (* the slide at LO, with the \
hard cross sections as functions of v at fixed s *)\n  (* for the pairs that \
observe the antiquark the TT square is the class's own with a <-> b, i.e. t \
<-> u (t -> -s - t with u eliminated) *)\n  slide = Table[With[{ttBorn = \
If[pair[\"Relabel\"], tt[\"Born\"][comp] /. u -> -s - t /. t -> -s - t, \
tt[\"Born\"][comp] /. u -> -s - t]},\n    \
Factor[(hard[transfer[\"Born\"][comp]] /. t -> -s (1 - v) /. colourRelation) \
-\n      (-signs[comp]) pair[\"Sign\"] pair[\"Factor\"] ((hard[ttBorn] /. t \
-> -s (1 - v)) /. v -> -v/(1 - v))/(1 - v) /. colourRelation] === 0], {comp, \
{\"XX\", \"NN\"}}];\n  Require[slide === {True, True}, \"The LO crossing \
relation of the hard cross sections fails\", pair[\"Name\"]];\n  (* the Born \
table: every transfer channel from a TT channel by the direct crossing *)\n  \
table = Association @ Table[name -> Module[{ch = \
StringSplit[StringReplace[name, \"->\" -> \"\"]], ttName, ttChannel, g},\n    \
  ttChannel = {ch[[1]], conjugate[ch[[3]]], conjugate[ch[[2]]]};\n      \
ttName = ttChannel[[1]] <> \" \" <> ttChannel[[2]] <> \" -> \" <> \
ttChannel[[3]];\n      Require[KeyExistsQ[tt[\"BornTable\"][\"XX\"], ttName], \
\"The TT Born table lacks the channel needed for \" <> name, ttName];\n      \
g = crossingSign[ch[[2]]] crossingFactor[ch[[2]]];\n      <|\"TT channel\" -> \
ttName, \"Factor\" -> g, \"Crossed\" -> Association @ Table[comp -> \
signs[comp] g (tt[\"BornTable\"][comp][ttName] /. \
crossingRules[momentumMap[False]]), {comp, {\"XX\", \"NN\"}}]|>],\n    {name, \
Keys[transfer[\"BornTable\"][\"XX\"]]}];\n  tableDifferences = Association @ \
Table[{name, comp} -> exactZero[table[name][\"Crossed\"][comp] - \
transfer[\"BornTable\"][comp][name]], {name, Keys[table]}, {comp, {\"XX\", \
\"NN\"}}];\n  Require[And @@ Values[tableDifferences], \"A crossed TT Born \
table entry differs from the transfer's\", Select[tableDifferences, # === \
False &]];\n  <|\"Born\" -> differences, \"Projections\" -> projections, \
\"SlideLO\" -> slide, \"BornTable\" -> Map[#[\"TT channel\"] &, table], \
\"CrossedTable\" -> Map[#[\"Crossed\"] &, table]|>];\nbornResults = \
Association @ Table[n -> bornCheck[loaded[n]], {n, \
pairList}];\nColumn[Table[loaded[n][\"Name\"] <> \": Born XX, NN and the \
table of \" <> ToString[Length[bornResults[n][\"BornTable\"]]] <> \" channels \
cross exactly\", {n, pairList}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Part A: the virtual interference", "Section"], 
  Cell["The family map: for each TT family, the crossed propagator momenta \
are matched, up to a shift and a reflection of the loop momentum, with a \
permutation of the propagators of one family of this process (the families \
are the same in both files, which is checked); the indices of \
KVirtual..[n1,n2,n3,n4] are permuted accordingly, the hat powers are \
unchanged.  The XX component is then compared coefficient by coefficient (the \
coefficient of every distinct integral x hat power), after dropping the \
scaleless integrals (those whose propagators with positive index have only \
vanishing differences of momenta); this term-by-term identity holds when both \
files route the graphs alike and is recorded, not required: the required \
comparison is the one after the reduction (next cell).", "Text"], 
  Cell["familyHeads = <|\"VirtualST\" -> KVirtualST, \"VirtualSU\" -> \
KVirtualSU, \"VirtualTU\" -> KVirtualTU|>;\nheadNames = Association[Reverse \
/@ Normal[familyHeads]];\nintegralHeads = Alternatives @@ \
Values[familyHeads];\nshifts = Flatten[Table[c1 pa + c2 pb + c3 p, {c1, -1, \
1}, {c2, -1, 1}, {c3, -1, 1}]];\nsameUpToSign[q1_, q2_] := Expand[q1 - q2] \
=== 0 || Expand[q1 + q2] === 0;\n(* {target family, sigma, delta, \
permutation}: propagator i of the crossed family is propagator \
permutation[[i]] of the target *)\nfamilyMap[families_, map_] := Association \
@ Table[name -> Module[{props = families[name] /. map, found},\n    found = \
Catch[Do[Module[{shifted = props /. loop -> sigma loop + delta, perm},\n      \
  perm = Table[FirstPosition[families[target], f_ /; sameUpToSign[f, q], \
{0}][[1]], {q, shifted}];\n        If[FreeQ[perm, 0] && Sort[perm] === \
Range[4], Throw[{target, sigma, delta, perm}]]],\n      {target, \
Keys[families]}, {sigma, {1, -1}}, {delta, shifts}]; None];\n    \
Require[found =!= None, \"No family of this process matches the crossed \
propagators of \" <> name, props]; found],\n  {name, \
Keys[families]}];\nintegralRules[fm_] := Table[With[{h = familyHeads[name], g \
= familyHeads[fm[name][[1]]], perm = fm[name][[4]]},\n  h[n__] :> g @@ \
Permute[{n}, InversePermutation[perm]]], {name, Keys[fm]}];\n(* the terms of \
a virtual expression grouped by integral and hat power: {integral, \
HatPower[h]} -> coefficient *)\nmonomials[expr_] := If[expr === 0, <||>, \
Module[{terms = With[{e = Expand[expr]}, Which[e === 0, {}, Head[e] === Plus, \
List @@ e, True, {e}]]},   (* a single product is one term *)\n  Association \
@ KeyValueMap[#1 -> Total[#2] &, GroupBy[terms,\n    Function[term, \
{FirstCase[term, integralHeads[__], None, {0, Infinity}], FirstCase[term, \
_HatPower, None, {0, Infinity}]}],\n    Function[term, term/(FirstCase[term, \
integralHeads[__], 1, {0, Infinity}] FirstCase[term, _HatPower, 1, {0, \
Infinity}])]]]]];\nscalelessQ[families_, (head_)[n__]] := Module[{q = \
families[headNames[head]], present = Flatten[Position[{n}, _?Positive]]},\n  \
And @@ Flatten[Table[squareOf[q[[i]] - q[[j]]] === 0, {i, present}, {j, \
present}]]];\ncompareMonomials[families_, a_, b_] := Module[{ma = \
monomials[a], mb = monomials[b], keys},\n  keys = Select[Union[Keys[ma], \
Keys[mb]], !scalelessQ[families, #[[1]]] &];\n  Select[Association @ Table[k \
-> Together[(Lookup[ma, Key[k], 0] - Lookup[mb, Key[k], 0]) /. \
colourRelation], {k, keys}], # =!= 0 &]];\ncrossVirtual[pair_, component_] := \
With[{tt = pair[\"TTAlgebra\"]},\n  crossObject[pair, \
ttComponents[tt[\"Virtual\"]][component] /. \
integralRules[familyMap[tt[\"Families\"], pair[\"Map\"]]], component] /. u -> \
-s - t];   (* 2 -> 2: u eliminated again (the composed map sends t to u) \
*)\nvirtualXXCheck[pair_] := Module[{tt = pair[\"TTAlgebra\"], transfer = \
pair[\"TransferAlgebra\"], fm, bad},\n  Require[tt[\"Families\"] === \
transfer[\"Families\"], \"The one-loop families of the two processes \
differ\"];\n  fm = familyMap[tt[\"Families\"], pair[\"Map\"]];\n  bad = \
compareMonomials[tt[\"Families\"], crossVirtual[pair, \"XX\"], \
transfer[\"Virtual\"][\"XX\"]];\n  (* identical term by term when both files \
route every graph onto the same family members; otherwise equal only up to \
integral identities (next cell) *)\n  <|\"FamilyMap\" -> fm, \"Integrals\" -> \
Length[monomials[transfer[\"Virtual\"][\"XX\"]]], \"TermByTerm\" -> (bad === \
<||>), \"DifferingTerms\" -> Length[bad]|>];\nvirtualXXResults = Association \
@ Table[n -> If[loaded[n][\"Spec\"][\"Virtual\"], virtualXXCheck[loaded[n]], \
<|\"FamilyMap\" -> None, \"TermByTerm\" -> \"no virtual correction\"|>], {n, \
pairList}];\nColumn[Table[loaded[n][\"Name\"] <> \": virtual XX identical \
term by term: \" <> ToString[virtualXXResults[n][\"TermByTerm\"]] <> \"; \
family map \" <>\n  ToString[If[virtualXXResults[n][\"FamilyMap\"] === None, \
None, Map[#[[1]] &, virtualXXResults[n][\"FamilyMap\"]]], InputForm], {n, \
pairList}]]", "Input"], Cell["The NN component contains the normal component \
of the loop momentum, which the two step-2 files reduce differently, and \
cannot be compared term by term.  Both sides are brought to a common form: \
every hatted power is replaced by its angular average over the \
(D-3)-dimensional space orthogonal to the scattering plane, loopHat2^h -> \
((D-4)/2)_h/((D-3)/2)_h (loop_perp^2)^h with loop_perp^2 = loop^2 - d.G^-1.d \
written through the inverse propagators of the family (so that a term becomes \
a sum of integrals with numerators); the union of the integrals of both sides \
is reduced by Kira (the families of kira/virtual, copied to \
Results/<route>/crossing/kira/class-<n>/virtual, with the seed ranges \
enlarged if the numerators need it) in D dimensions, the masters are \
identified by their values (bubble of one channel, box of a pair of channels, \
as in step 3, since the same bubble can be a master of two families), and \
their coefficients must agree exactly as rational functions of s, t, D, CA, \
Nf.  The XX component is passed through the same reduction: this is the \
required check for XX as well.", "Text"], Cell["loopSymbols = {L2, Lpa, Lpb, \
Lp};\ngram = {{0, s/2, -t/2}, {s/2, 0, -u/2}, {-t/2, -u/2, 0}} /. u -> -s - \
t;\ninverseProps[families_, name_] := inverseProps[families, name] = \
Module[{sol},\n  sol = Solve[Table[Dj[j] == (squareOf[families[name][[j]]] /. \
u -> -s - t), {j, 4}], loopSymbols];\n  Require[Length[sol] == 1, \"Cannot \
express the loop scalar products through the propagators of \" <> name]; \
First[sol]];\nloopPerp2[families_, name_] := loopPerp2[families, name] = \
Factor[(L2 - {Lpa, Lpb, Lp} . Inverse[gram] . {Lpa, Lpb, Lp}) /. \
inverseProps[families, name]];\nperpMoment[h_] := Pochhammer[(D - 4)/2, \
h]/Pochhammer[(D - 3)/2, h];\n(* every integral x HatPower[h] -> moment x sum \
of integrals with the numerator (loop_perp^2)^h *)\ndehat[families_, expr_] \
:= Total[KeyValueMap[Function[{key, coefficient}, With[{k = key[[1]], h = \
key[[2]][[1]]},\n  If[h == 0, coefficient k,\n    coefficient perpMoment[h] \
Total[(#[[2]] (Head[k] @@ (List @@ k - #[[1]])) &) /@ \
CoefficientRules[Expand[loopPerp2[families, headNames[Head[k]]]^h], Array[Dj, \
4]]]]]],\n  monomials[expr]]];\nvirtualHeads = {KVirtualST -> \"virtual_ST\", \
KVirtualSU -> \"virtual_SU\", KVirtualTU -> \
\"virtual_TU\"};\nreduceBoth[pair_, components_] := Module[{families = \
pair[\"TTAlgebra\"][\"Families\"], sides, targets, rMax, sMax, kiraDir, jobs, \
rules, masters, keys},\n  sides = Association @ Table[comp -> \
{dehat[families, crossVirtual[pair, comp]], dehat[families, \
pair[\"TransferAlgebra\"][\"Virtual\"][comp]]}, {comp, components}];\n  \
targets = Union[Cases[sides, integralHeads[__], Infinity]];\n  rMax = \
Max[Total[Select[List @@ #, Positive]] & /@ targets]; sMax = \
Max[-Total[Select[List @@ #, Negative]] & /@ targets];\n  kiraDir = \
PrepareKira[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"kira\", \"virtual\"}], \
FileNameJoin[{crossingDirectory, \"kira\", \"class-\" <> pair[\"Transfer\"], \
\"virtual\"}]];\n  jobs = FileNameJoin[{kiraDir, \"jobs.yaml\"}];\n  \
Export[jobs, StringReplace[Import[jobs, \"Text\"], \"r: 7, s: 4\" -> \"r: \" \
<> ToString[Max[7, rMax]] <> \", s: \" <> ToString[Max[4, sMax]]], \
\"Text\"];\n  WriteKiraTargets[kiraDir, targets, virtualHeads];\n  \
RunKira[kiraDir];\n  rules = RestoreScale[Join @@ Table[KiraRules[kiraDir, \
name, virtualHeads], {name, Select[Values[virtualHeads], \
FileExistsQ[FileNameJoin[{kiraDir, \"results\", #, \"kira_targets.m\"}]] \
&]}], s, {t -> t/s}, Keys[virtualHeads]];\n  sides = Map[Collect[Expand[# /. \
Dispatch[rules] /. d -> D], integralHeads[__], Together] &, sides, {2}];\n  \
masters = Union[Cases[sides, integralHeads[__], Infinity]];\n  (* a target \
that is itself a master has no rule: what remains must be bubbles and boxes \
(indices 0 and 1 only), as in step 3 *)\n  Require[And @@ (SubsetQ[{0, 1}, \
List @@ #] & /@ masters), \"Some integrals were not reduced by Kira\", \
Select[masters, !SubsetQ[{0, 1}, List @@ #] &]];\n  (* masters of different \
families with the same value (a bubble of one channel, the box of one pair of \
channels) are identified by their value, as in step 3 *)\n  sides = \
Map[Collect[# /. Dispatch[Table[m -> masterValue[families, m], {m, \
masters}]], _bubble | _box | _triangle, Together] &, sides, {2}];\n  keys = \
Union[Cases[sides, _bubble | _box | _triangle, Infinity]];\n  <|\"Targets\" \
-> Length[targets], \"Ranges\" -> {rMax, sMax}, \"Masters\" -> masters, \
\"MasterValues\" -> keys,\n    \"Differences\" -> Association @ Table[comp -> \
Select[Association @ Table[m -> Together[(Coefficient[sides[comp][[1]], m] - \
Coefficient[sides[comp][[2]], m]) /. colourRelation], {m, keys}], # =!= 0 &], \
{comp, components}]|>];\n(* the value of a master (indices 0, 1): bubble[P^2] \
of the momentum through its two propagators, box[{S, T}] of its two channels \
(symmetric), with u = -s - t *)\nmasterValue[families_, (head_)[n__]] := \
Module[{q = families[headNames[head]], present = Flatten[Position[{n}, 1]], \
inv},\n  inv[x_] := Factor[squareOf[x] /. u -> -s - t];\n  \
Switch[Length[present],\n    2, bubble[inv[q[[present[[1]]]] - \
q[[present[[2]]]]]],\n    4, box[Sort[{inv[q[[3]] - q[[1]]], inv[q[[4]] - \
q[[2]]]}]],\n    _, triangle[Sort[Table[inv[q[[present[[i]]]] - \
q[[present[[Mod[i, Length[present]] + 1]]]]], {i, \
Length[present]}]]]]];\nvirtualNNResults = Association @ Table[n -> \
If[loaded[n][\"Spec\"][\"Virtual\"], reduceBoth[loaded[n], {\"NN\", \"XX\"}], \
\"no virtual correction in this class\"], {n, \
pairList}];\nDo[Require[!AssociationQ[virtualNNResults[n]] || And @@ (# === \
<||> & /@ Values[virtualNNResults[n][\"Differences\"]]),\n  \"The crossed TT \
virtual NN (or XX) differs from the transfer's after the reduction to master \
integrals\", {loaded[n][\"Name\"], virtualNNResults[n][\"Differences\"]}], \
{n, pairList}];\nColumn[Table[loaded[n][\"Name\"] <> \": \" <> \
If[AssociationQ[virtualNNResults[n]],\n  \"virtual NN and XX agree exactly on \
\" <> ToString[Length[virtualNNResults[n][\"MasterValues\"]]] <> \" distinct \
master integrals \" <> ToString[virtualNNResults[n][\"MasterValues\"], \
InputForm] <> \" (\" <> ToString[virtualNNResults[n][\"Targets\"]] <> \" \
targets)\", virtualNNResults[n]], {n, pairList}]]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Part A: the real emission", "Section"], 
  Cell["The crossed TT real-emission square (XX and NN, and the two \
projections) against the transfer's, exactly at random rational points of s, \
t, u, A, B (C = -s4 - A - B), D, CA, spe3, Nf: the expressions have tens of \
thousands of terms and are not brought to a common denominator.  The \
reference vectors of the gluon polarization sums differ between the two files \
(the TT's k2 uses pb, i.e. -p after the crossing; the transfer's uses pb), \
which is immaterial for the complete squares (gauge invariance, checked in \
both step-2 files).", "Text"], Cell["realPoints = Table[With[{r = \
RandomInteger[{1, 97}, 8]/RandomInteger[{98, 197}, 8]},\n  {s -> 1, t -> \
-r[[1]], u -> -r[[2]] (1 - r[[1]]), A -> -r[[3]], B -> -r[[4]], D -> 4 - \
r[[5]], CA -> 2 + 10 r[[6]], spe3 -> r[[7]], Nf -> 5}], {3}];\natPoint[expr_, \
point_] := Together[expr /. C -> -(s + t + u) - A - B /. colourRelation /. \
point];\nrealCheck[pair_] := Module[{tt = \
ttComponents[pair[\"TTAlgebra\"][\"Real\"]], transfer = \
pair[\"TransferAlgebra\"][\"Real\"], differences, projections},\n  \
differences = Association @ Table[comp -> Table[atPoint[crossObject[pair, \
tt[comp], comp] - transfer[comp], point], {point, realPoints}], {comp, \
{\"XX\", \"NN\"}}];\n  Require[And @@ (# === {0, 0, 0} & /@ \
Values[differences]), \"The crossed TT real-emission square differs from the \
transfer's\", {pair[\"Name\"], differences}];\n  projections = \
{Table[atPoint[-pair[\"Sign\"] pair[\"Factor\"] \
(pair[\"TTAlgebra\"][\"Real\"][\"TT\"] /. pair[\"Rules\"]) - \
(transfer[\"XX\"] + transfer[\"NN\"])/2, point], {point, realPoints}],\n    \
Table[atPoint[-pair[\"Sign\"] pair[\"Factor\"] \
(pair[\"TTAlgebra\"][\"Real\"][\"Symmetric\"] /. pair[\"Rules\"]) - \
(transfer[\"XX\"] - transfer[\"NN\"])/2, point], {point, realPoints}]};\n  \
Require[projections === {{0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 0}}, \"The TT projections of the \
real emission do not cross into -(XX+NN)/2 and -(XX-NN)/2\", \
pair[\"Name\"]];\n  <|\"Real\" -> differences, \"Projections\" -> \
projections, \"LeafCounts\" -> LeafCount /@ transfer|>];\nrealResults = \
Association @ Table[n -> realCheck[loaded[n]], {n, \
pairList}];\nColumn[Table[loaded[n][\"Name\"] <> \": real emission XX and NN \
cross exactly at \" <> ToString[Length[realPoints]] <> \" rational points\", \
{n, pairList}]]", "Input"], Cell["Part A is saved per pair (the map, the \
factor, the family map, the checks), before Part B.", "Text"], 
  Cell["partA = Association @ Table[n -> <|\"Pair\" -> loaded[n][\"Name\"], \
\"Transfer\" -> n, \"TT\" -> loaded[n][\"TT\"], \"Map\" -> \
loaded[n][\"Map\"], \"Rules\" -> loaded[n][\"Rules\"], \"Factor\" -> \
loaded[n][\"Factor\"], \"Sign\" -> loaded[n][\"Sign\"],\n  \"Signs\" -> \
signs, \"Born\" -> bornResults[n], \"VirtualXX\" -> virtualXXResults[n], \
\"VirtualReduced\" -> virtualNNResults[n], \"Real\" -> realResults[n], \
\"Route\" -> route,\n  \"Projections\" -> \"-sigma g x TT -> (XX+NN)/2, \
-sigma g x Symmetric -> (XX-NN)/2 of the transfer process\"|>, {n, \
pairList}];\nDo[SaveResult[\"class-\" <> n, <|\"PartA\" -> partA[n], \
\"PartB\" -> \"not run\"|>, route <> \"/crossing\"], {n, pairList}];\n\"Part \
A saved for \" <> StringRiffle[pairList, \", \"]", "Input"], 
  Cell["Part B: the pseudo-classes", "Section"], 
  Cell["The crossed TT algebra is written as \
Results/<route>/class-<n>x/Algebra.wl in the format of step 2 of this \
process: Born, Virtual and Real with the components XX and NN (the crossed TT \
objects with their factors; the virtual with the families relabelled), the \
Born table crossed from the TT table (equal to the transfer's by Part A), the \
class entry of classes.wl as the specification.  Steps 3 and 4 of this \
process are then run on the pseudo-class in fresh kernels (RunSteps, with the \
override class=<n>x; skipped when their results exist and reuse = \"yes\"): \
step 3 integrates the crossed integrands in the transfer region, step 4 \
assembles them with the transfer counterterms and requires the cancellation \
of the poles.", "Text"], Cell["pseudoName[n_] := n <> \
\"x\";\nwritePseudoClass[pair_] := Module[{tt = pair[\"TTAlgebra\"], n = \
pair[\"Transfer\"], algebra},\n  algebra = <|\"Born\" -> Association @ \
Table[comp -> Factor[crossObject[pair, tt[\"Born\"][comp], comp] /. u -> -s - \
t], {comp, {\"XX\", \"NN\"}}],\n    \"Virtual\" -> Association @ Table[comp \
-> Collect[crossVirtual[pair, comp], {integralHeads[__], _HatPower}, Factor], \
{comp, {\"XX\", \"NN\"}}],\n    \"Real\" -> Association @ Table[comp -> \
crossObject[pair, ttComponents[tt[\"Real\"]][comp], comp], {comp, {\"XX\", \
\"NN\"}}],\n    \"BornTable\" -> Association @ Table[comp -> Map[#[comp] &, \
bornResults[n][\"CrossedTable\"]], {comp, {\"XX\", \"NN\"}}],\n    \"Class\" \
-> pseudoName[n], \"Spec\" -> pair[\"Spec\"], \"Spins\" -> {\"XX\", \"NN\"}, \
\"Families\" -> tt[\"Families\"],\n    \"Variables\" -> tt[\"Variables\"] <> \
\"; crossed from HadronicTT class \" <> pair[\"TT\"] <> \" with \" <> \
ToString[pair[\"Rules\"], InputForm] <> \", factor \" <> \
ToString[pair[\"Sign\"] pair[\"Factor\"], InputForm] <> \" and the signs XX: \
-1, NN: +1\",\n    \"Origin\" -> \
\"Processes/HadronicTransfer/5-Crossing.wl\"|>;\n  SaveResult[\"Algebra\", \
algebra, route <> \"/class-\" <> \
pseudoName[n]]];\nDo[writePseudoClass[loaded[n]], {n, \
pairList}];\n\"pseudo-classes written: \" <> StringRiffle[pseudoName /@ \
pairList, \", \"]", "Input"], Cell["pseudoResultsValidQ[n_, started_: None] \
:= Module[{choices, files, receipts, algebraFile, reducedFile, resultFile,\n  \
  algebraHash, reducedHash, resultHash, root, relative, bound},\n  choices = \
{{\"route\", route}, {\"class\", pseudoName[n]}};\n  files = \
FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], #}] & /@ {\"3-Reduce.wl\", \
\"4-Transfer.wl\"};\n  If[!And @@ (StepReceiptValidQ[#, choices, started] & \
/@ files), Return[False]];\n  receipts = \
Import[FileNameJoin[{ResultsDirectory[], FileBaseName[#] <> \"-\" <> route <> \
\"-\" <> pseudoName[n] <> \".receipt.json\"}], \"RawJSON\"] & /@ files;\n  \
{algebraFile, reducedFile, resultFile} = transferFile[pseudoName[n], #] & /@ \
{\"Algebra\", \"Reduced\", \"Transfer\"};\n  If[!And @@ (FileExistsQ /@ \
{algebraFile, reducedFile, resultFile}), Return[False]];\n  \
If[NumberQ[started] && !And @@ (AbsoluteTime[FileDate[#]] >= Floor[started] & \
/@ {reducedFile, resultFile}), Return[False]];\n  {algebraHash, reducedHash, \
resultHash} = IntegerString[FileHash[#, \"SHA256\"], 16, 64] & /@ \
{algebraFile, reducedFile, resultFile};\n  root = \
StringReplace[ExpandFileName[$FeynFacetDirectory], $PathnameSeparator ~~ \
EndOfString -> \"\"];\n  relative[file_] := StringDrop[ExpandFileName[file], \
StringLength[root] + 1];\n  bound[receipt_, kind_, file_, hash_] := \
Lookup[receipt[\"provenance\"][kind], relative[file], None] === hash;\n  \
bound[receipts[[1]], \"inputs\", algebraFile, algebraHash] &&\n    \
bound[receipts[[1]], \"outputs\", reducedFile, reducedHash] &&\n    \
bound[receipts[[2]], \"inputs\", algebraFile, algebraHash] &&\n    \
bound[receipts[[2]], \"inputs\", reducedFile, reducedHash] &&\n    \
bound[receipts[[2]], \"outputs\", resultFile, \
resultHash]];\nrunPseudoClass[n_] := Module[{summary, rows, started},\n  \
If[reuse === \"yes\" && pseudoResultsValidQ[n], Return[\"reused\"]];\n  \
started = AbsoluteTime[];\n  summary = RunSteps[\"HadronicTransfer\", route, \
{3, 4}, \"class=\" <> pseudoName[n]];\n  rows = If[Head[summary] === Grid, \
Rest[First[summary]], {}];\n  Require[MatchQ[rows, {{\"3-Reduce\", \
\"passed\", _}, {\"4-Transfer\", \"passed\", _}}],\n    \"Steps 3 and 4 of \
the pseudo-class must both finish successfully\", {pseudoName[n], \
summary}];\n  Require[pseudoResultsValidQ[n, started],\n    \"The \
pseudo-class needs fresh receipts binding Algebra, Reduced and Transfer\", \
pseudoName[n]];\n  summary];\npseudoRuns = If[stage === \"all\", Association \
@ Table[n -> runPseudoClass[n], {n, pairList}], \"stage A: steps 3 and 4 of \
the pseudo-classes not run\"];\npseudoRuns", "Input"], 
  Cell["Part B: the NLO comparison", "Section"], 
  Cell["The hard coefficients of the pseudo-class (Transfer.wl of class <n>x) \
against those of the directly computed class <n>, both components: the Born \
term (exactly), the finite real-emission tuple and the finite virtual term \
separately, the counterterm tuples, and the complete finite coefficients \
{regular, D0, D1, delta} (with the SU(N) colour relation; the comparison is \
exact at rational points of s, v, w, Nf with the three scales symbolic, \
ExactDifference; a numerical difference to 30 digits is recorded as well).  \
The difference of the two components of the pseudo-class equals, by \
construction, -2 sigma g times the crossed evanescent Symmetric projection of \
HadronicTT assembled with the transfer counterterms; whether it vanishes (as \
the TT Symmetric remainder does) is reported with the result, evaluated to 30 \
digits at the physical points (the expression holds logarithms of rational \
numbers that Simplify does not combine).  The pole cancellation of the \
pseudo-class was required by step 4 itself; its receipt is recorded.", 
   "Text"], Cell["scaleAssumptions = muR > 0 && muF > 0 && muFF > 0 && s > \
0;\nexactPoints = Map[Select[#, FreeQ[#[[1]], muR | muF | muFF] &] &, \
PhysicalPoints];            (* s, v, w, Nf rational; the scales symbolic \
*)\n(* the difference of two scalars or tuples at one point: Together, \
PowerExpand of the scale logarithms, Simplify, and FullSimplify only if \
needed *)\ndifferenceAt[a_, b_, point_] := Module[{d = Together[(a - b) /. \
colourRelation /. point]},\n  d = Simplify[PowerExpand[d, Assumptions -> \
scaleAssumptions], scaleAssumptions];\n  If[d =!= 0, d = \
FullSimplify[FunctionExpand[d], scaleAssumptions]]; d];\nexactDifferences[a_, \
b_] := Table[differenceAt[x[[1]], x[[2]], point], {point, exactPoints}, {x, \
Transpose[{Flatten[{a}], Flatten[{b}]}]}];\nnloCheck[n_] := Module[{ours, \
theirs, receipt, born, real, virtual, counterterms, finite, numeric, \
componentDifference},\n  Require[FileExistsQ[transferFile[n, \"Transfer\"]], \
\"Transfer.wl of class \" <> n <> \" (step 4 of this process) is needed for \
the NLO comparison\"];\n  ours = Get[transferFile[pseudoName[n], \
\"Transfer\"]]; theirs = Get[transferFile[n, \"Transfer\"]];\n  receipt = \
With[{file = FileNameJoin[{ResultsDirectory[], \"4-Transfer-\" <> route <> \
\"-\" <> pseudoName[n] <> \".receipt.json\"}]}, If[FileExistsQ[file], \
Import[file, \"RawJSON\"][\"completed\"], \"no receipt\"]];\n  born = \
Association @ Table[spin -> Simplify[(ours[\"Born\"][spin] - \
theirs[\"Born\"][spin]) /. colourRelation], {spin, {\"XX\", \"NN\"}}];\n  \
Require[And @@ (# === 0 & /@ Values[born]), \"The Born terms differ\", {n, \
born}];\n  real = Association @ Table[spin -> \
exactDifferences[ours[\"Real\"][spin], theirs[\"Real\"][spin]], {spin, \
{\"XX\", \"NN\"}}];\n  virtual = Association @ Table[spin -> \
exactDifferences[ours[\"Virtual\"][spin], theirs[\"Virtual\"][spin]], {spin, \
{\"XX\", \"NN\"}}];\n  counterterms = Association @ Table[spin -> Association \
@ Table[key -> exactDifferences[ours[\"Counterterms\"][spin][key], \
theirs[\"Counterterms\"][spin][key]], {key, \
Keys[theirs[\"Counterterms\"][spin]]}], {spin, {\"XX\", \"NN\"}}];\n  finite \
= Association @ Table[spin -> exactDifferences[ours[\"Finite\"][spin], \
theirs[\"Finite\"][spin]], {spin, {\"XX\", \"NN\"}}];\n  numeric = \
Association @ Table[spin -> NumericDifference[ours[\"Finite\"][spin] /. \
colourRelation /. CA -> 3, theirs[\"Finite\"][spin] /. colourRelation /. CA \
-> 3, PhysicalPoints, 30], {spin, {\"XX\", \"NN\"}}];\n  (* XX - NN of the \
pseudo-class (= that of the class, by the comparison above), at 30 digits: \
its logarithms of numbers are not combined by Simplify *)\n  \
componentDifference = NumericDifference[ours[\"ComponentDifference\"] /. \
colourRelation /. CA -> 3, 0 ours[\"ComponentDifference\"], PhysicalPoints, \
30];\n  Require[And @@ (# === 0 & /@ Flatten[Values[real]]), \"The finite \
real-emission parts differ\", {n, real}];\n  Require[And @@ (# === 0 & /@ \
Flatten[Values[virtual]]), \"The finite virtual parts differ\", {n, \
virtual}];\n  Require[And @@ (# === 0 & /@ Flatten[Values[Map[Values, \
counterterms]]]), \"The counterterms differ\", {n, counterterms}];\n  \
Require[And @@ (# === 0 & /@ Flatten[Values[finite]]), \"The finite hard \
coefficients of the pseudo-class differ from the directly computed ones\", \
{n, finite}];\n  <|\"PseudoClass\" -> pseudoName[n], \"Step4Completed\" -> \
receipt, \"Born\" -> born, \"Real\" -> real, \"Virtual\" -> virtual, \
\"Counterterms\" -> counterterms, \"Finite\" -> finite,\n    \
\"NumericFinite\" -> numeric, \"ComponentDifference\" -> componentDifference, \
\"Points\" -> exactPoints|>];\npartB = If[stage === \"all\", Association @ \
Table[n -> nloCheck[n], {n, pairList}], \"stage A: no NLO \
comparison\"];\nIf[AssociationQ[partB], Column[Table[loaded[n][\"Name\"] <> \
\": NLO finite coefficients of XX and NN agree exactly at \" <> \
ToString[Length[exactPoints]] <> \" points; poles of the pseudo-class \
cancelled (step 4 completed: \" <>\n  ToString[partB[n][\"Step4Completed\"]] \
<> \"); XX - NN of the transfer class at three points (30 digits): \" <> \
ToString[partB[n][\"ComponentDifference\"], InputForm], {n, pairList}]], \
partB]", "Input"], Cell["Save and summary", "Section"], 
  Cell["Do[SaveResult[\"class-\" <> n, <|\"PartA\" -> partA[n], \"PartB\" -> \
If[AssociationQ[partB], partB[n], partB], \"Stage\" -> stage|>, route <> \
\"/crossing\"], {n, pairList}];\nsummary = Association @ Table[With[{file = \
FileNameJoin[{crossingDirectory, \"class-\" <> n <> \".wl\"}]}, n -> \
If[FileExistsQ[file], With[{r = Get[file]},\n  <|\"Pair\" -> \
r[\"PartA\"][\"Pair\"], \"Factor\" -> r[\"PartA\"][\"Sign\"] \
r[\"PartA\"][\"Factor\"], \"Part A\" -> \"passed\", \"Part B\" -> \
If[AssociationQ[r[\"PartB\"]], \"passed (finite XX, NN equal)\", \
r[\"PartB\"]]|>], \"not run\"]], {n, \
Keys[crossingTable]}];\nDataset[summary]", "Input"]}, 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 800}]
